MAMUT-routing: let HGS-CVRP read an explicit (possibly asymmetric) distance matrix.

HGS-CVRP's search handles asymmetric distances (its README; the 2-opt moves keep reversal
costs), and Params takes a full matrix: only the CVRPLIB reader is coordinate-only. With
this patch the reader also accepts EDGE_WEIGHT_FORMAT : FULL_MATRIX and an
EDGE_WEIGHT_SECTION (row i = costs from node i), keeps NODE_COORD_SECTION for the polar
sectors of SWAP*, and computes Euclidean distances only when no matrix was given.

Against github.com/vidalt/HGS-CVRP 1a92795. Apply and build:

    git -C HGS-CVRP apply /path/to/hgs-cvrp-explicit-matrix.patch
    cmake -S HGS-CVRP -B HGS-CVRP/build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake --build HGS-CVRP/build

`mamut-routing solvers list` prints this file's installed path in the hgs-cvrp hint.

